{"name":"Bubbly","hex":"#ead8c0","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bubbly","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Full of bubbles.","Cheerful, lively."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Champagne."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bubbly"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bubbly","blocks":[{"text":"\"Bubbly\" is the debut single of American singer-songwriter Colbie Caillat from her first album, Coco (2007). Written by Caillat and Jason Reeves and produced by Mikal Blue, the song was released as the album's lead single on May 15, 2007. \"Bubbly\" is Caillat's only song to peak within the top 10 of the US Billboard Hot 100; it remains her highest-charting song. Internationally, \"Bubbly\" reached number one in Australia, Brazil, and the Czech Republic. It also became a top-10 hit in several European countries, including Belgium, Germany, and Norway, as well as Japan and New Zealand. It is certified six-times platinum in the US and Australia as well as gold or higher in six additional countries."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f5/Bubbly_%28Colbie_Caillat%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bubbly","wikidata":"Q2552843"},{"title":"Bubbly (Young Thug, Drake and Travis Scott song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Bubbly\" is a song by American rappers Young Thug and Travis Scott and Canadian rapper Drake. It was sent to US rhythmic radio through YSL Records and 300 Entertainment as the lead and only single from the former's second studio album, Punk, on November 2, 2021. The three artists wrote the song with producers Wheezy, Cardo, Dez Wright, Yung Exclusive, Johnny Juliano, and Mu Lean."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/80/BubblyYoungThug.jpg/330px-BubblyYoungThug.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bubbly_(Young_Thug%2C_Drake_and_Travis_Scott_song)","wikidata":"Q109284952"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"bubbly":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9b/En-us-bubbly.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/9/9b/En-us-bubbly.ogg/En-us-bubbly.ogg.mp3"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Bubbly packaging","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Bubbly_packaging.jpg/500px-Bubbly_packaging.jpg","ratio":1.3333333333333333,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bubbly_packaging.jpg","share":0.3025},{"title":"Grey heron (00129p)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg/500px-Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg","ratio":0.8691693290734824,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grey_heron_(00129p).jpg","share":0.286875},{"title":"Glass of sparkling wine","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Glass_of_sparkling_wine.jpg/500px-Glass_of_sparkling_wine.jpg","ratio":0.75,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Glass_of_sparkling_wine.jpg","share":0.19125},{"title":"Flight of sparkling wine","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Flight_of_sparkling_wine.jpg/500px-Flight_of_sparkling_wine.jpg","ratio":1.3333333333333333,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flight_of_sparkling_wine.jpg","share":0.0875},{"title":"Luxor Sparkling Wine","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Luxor_Sparkling_Wine.jpg/500px-Luxor_Sparkling_Wine.jpg","ratio":0.585982478097622,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Luxor_Sparkling_Wine.jpg","share":0.084375},{"title":"Two glasses of sparking wine and bottle in home kitchen","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Two_glasses_of_sparking_wine_and_bottle_in_home_kitchen.jpg/500px-Two_glasses_of_sparking_wine_an